[English Terms]

All contents of this repository — including but not limited to the
game program (HTML / JavaScript), narrative and lorebook texts, UI
and visual design, city blueprints and generation logic,
runtime-converted 3D models and textures, music files, screenshots,
and documentation — are proprietary works protected by copyright
law. This file is NOT an open-source license and grants no
open-source rights.

1. Permitted

  1. Online play: playing the game via the official page at
     https://rome-olive.vercel.app/.
  2. Personal offline play: running this work on your own devices
     for your own play.
  3. Sharing links: sharing the repository URL or the online play
     URL with others.

2. Prohibited (without prior written permission from the copyright
   holder)

  1. Copying, modifying, or translating this work, or creating any
     derivative works (including fan remakes, modified versions,
     re-skins, or ports to other languages or platforms).
  2. Redistributing any file in this repository in any form,
     including mirroring, re-uploading, or repackaging to other
     platforms or file-sharing services.
  3. Using this work or any part of it for any commercial purpose.
  4. Extracting, decrypting, converting, or separately using the 3D
     models, textures, music, or other assets contained in this work
     (see Section 3).
  5. Removing or altering this notice or any copyright information
     within the work.

3. Third-Party Assets

  The 3D models, textures, and music used at runtime are not
  original to this project; their copyrights belong to their
  respective rights holders. Such assets exist in this repository
  only in the converted and packaged form required for runtime
  presentation in the browser. They are not offered as an asset
  library, and no right of reuse is granted:

  1. 3D models and textures originate from commercial asset packs
     and remain bound by their original vendors' license terms.
  2. Rights in the musical recordings and compositions belong to
     their respective holders; they are used solely as background
     music for this game.
  3. No one may extract, restore, or repurpose these assets from
     this repository. To use them, obtain a license from the
     original rights holders yourself.
  4. Should any rights holder object to the use of an asset in this
     project, the material in question will be removed.

4. Regarding AI

  This work is a purely client-side, static front-end. It does not
  include, provide, proxy, or resell any artificial intelligence
  service. Any third-party AI endpoint a player connects to is
  configured at that player's sole discretion; all costs incurred
  and all content generated thereby are that player's sole
  responsibility and are unrelated to this project.

5. Miscellaneous

  1. The public hosting of this repository on GitHub exists solely
     to provide an online play channel, and does not constitute any
     authorization of the prohibited acts above.
  2. Forking as permitted by the GitHub Terms of Service is limited
     to viewing within the GitHub platform and confers none of the
     rights prohibited by these terms.
  3. This work is provided "AS IS", without warranty of any kind,
     express or implied.
  4. For permissions beyond these terms (e.g., derivative works,
     redistribution, commercial use), please contact the copyright
     holder via this repository's Issues page.
